      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:3:5",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ وَ اللَّهِ لَوْ مَلَكْتُ مِنْ أَمْرِ النَّاسِ شَيْئاً لَأَقَمْتُهُمْ بِالسَّيْفِ وَ السَّوْطِ حَتَّى يُطَلِّقُوا لِلْعِدَّةِ كَمَا أَمَرَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from one of our companions, from Aban, from Abu Baseer who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘By Allah<sup>azwj</sup>! If I<sup>asws</sup> owned anything from the affairs of the people, I<sup>asws</sup> would straighten them by the sword and the whip until they would be divorcing to the waiting period just as Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic has Commanded’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from certain persons of our people from Aban from abu Basir who has said the following: “I once heard abu Ja‘far, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, saying, ‘Had the affairs of people been in my hands I would straighten them with the sword and whip until they divorced with waiting period as Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, has commanded.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
